#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""One-file builder for the Macro Early-Warning Monitor (FRED).

Plain ASCII (the code rides inside as base64), so it survives corporate
email/DLP intact. Run it on the target machine and it BUILDS the workbook
locally -- nothing binary is ever transmitted.

USAGE (PowerShell):
    python -m pip install pandas openpyxl
    python build_macro_monitor.py

It writes into the current folder:
    Macro_Early_Warning_Monitor.xlsm           (macro embedded, demo-populated)
    Macro_Early_Warning_Monitor_fallback.xlsx  (no VBA; if Excel rejects the .xlsm,
                      open this, paste macro.bas via Alt+F11, save as .xlsm)
    runner.py, macro.bas, requirements.txt

Refresh later (workbook CLOSED):
    python runner.py --workbook ".\\Macro_Early_Warning_Monitor.xlsm" --demo    # offline demo
    $env:FRED_API_KEY = "yourkey"                       # live FRED needs a key
    python runner.py --workbook ".\\Macro_Early_Warning_Monitor.xlsm"           # live FRED
Or drop control_center.py next to it and run: python control_center.py
"""
